    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>An <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#ionia">Ionian Greek</a> port near the mouth of the Cayster, founded by tradition c. 1000 BCE and famed for its sanctuary of Artemis.</li><li>The Artemision acted as bank, refuge and pilgrimage centre; its rebuilt temple was one of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World.</li><li>Ephesus passed from Lydian, Persian, Athenian and Hellenistic overlords to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#rome">Rome</a> in 133 BCE and became the chief city of Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#asia">Asia</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>A deposit beneath the Temple of Artemis contained some of the oldest coins ever found, small lumps of electrum from around 600 BCE.</p></aside>
    </section>

